COMMENT ON ROLE app IS 'Default permissions granted to the applications.';
COMMENT ON ROLE financial_app IS 'User the Financial application connects with.';

COMMENT ON TABLE account.balances IS '[CONFIDENTIAL] Table used to persist the balance of each ledger account.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.balances.id IS '[NONE] The balance identifier generated by the database (e.g., 1).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.balances.number IS '[NONE] The ledger account number, unique per balance (e.g., 2.1.1.001).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.balances.balance IS '[CONFIDENTIAL] The account balance as a signed decimal with two places (e.g., -50.00).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.balances.currency IS '[NONE] The balance currency in ISO 4217 format (e.g., BRL).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.balances.updated_at IS '[NONE] The UTC date and time when the balance last changed in ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2026-02-13T08:49:44.931408+00:00).';

COMMENT ON TABLE bookkeeping.transactions IS '[CONFIDENTIAL] Table used to persist the events the financial transactions raised, appended only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bookkeeping.transactions.code IS '[NONE] The event identifier in UUID format, which is also the Kafka message key (e.g., 4fc06d14-0a42-41af-8d78-710b2a60947d).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bookkeeping.transactions.payload IS '[CONFIDENTIAL] The event payload as JSON (e.g., {"id":"4fc06d14-0a42-41af-8d78-710b2a60947d","status":1}).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bookkeeping.transactions.revision IS '[NONE] The revision of the shape of the event payload, a positive number (e.g., 1).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bookkeeping.transactions.sequence IS '[NONE] The order of the event among the events of the same aggregate, a positive number (e.g., 1).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bookkeeping.transactions.event_name IS '[NONE] The name of the event (e.g., TransactionRegistered).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bookkeeping.transactions.occurred_on IS '[NONE] The UTC date and time when the event occurred in ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2026-02-13T08:49:44.931408+00:00).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bookkeeping.transactions.aggregate_id IS '[NONE] The identifier of the aggregate that raised the event (e.g., 4fc06d14-0a42-41af-8d78-710b2a60947d).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN bookkeeping.transactions.aggregate_type IS '[NONE] The name of the aggregate that raised the event (e.g., Transaction).';

COMMENT ON TABLE account.troubleshoot IS '[CONFIDENTIAL] Table used to persist the policy reactions that failed until a replay of each one succeeds.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.troubleshoot.id IS '[NONE] The failure identifier in UUID format (e.g., e8985137-26d4-4286-8b46-4fd86c306c4c).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.troubleshoot.error IS '[NONE] The cause of the last failure in business terms, or its full trace when it is not a known one (e.g., Account with number 9.9.9.999 not found).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.troubleshoot.resent IS '[NONE] The flag that marks the failure as replayed with success, 1 when it was and 0 while it is pending (e.g., 0).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.troubleshoot.payload IS '[CONFIDENTIAL] The payload of the event as the policy received it, kept as text so a malformed one is recorded too (e.g., {"id":"4fc06d14-0a42-41af-8d78-710b2a60947d"}).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.troubleshoot.created_at IS '[NONE] The UTC date and time when the failure was recorded in ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2026-02-13T08:49:44.931408+00:00).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.troubleshoot.updated_at IS '[NONE] The UTC date and time of the last replay in ISO 8601 format, null until the first replay (e.g., 2026-02-13T08:49:44.931408+00:00).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.troubleshoot.event_name IS '[NONE] The fully qualified name of the event the policy failed on (e.g., financial.accounting.account.driver.policies.events.TransactionRegistered).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.troubleshoot.policy_name IS '[NONE] The fully qualified name of the policy that failed (e.g., financial.accounting.account.driver.policies.AdjustBalancePolicy).';

COMMENT ON TABLE account.adjustments IS 'Table used to persist the transactions whose balance adjustment was applied, so a replayed event changes nothing.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.adjustments.transaction_id IS '[NONE] The identifier of the transaction whose adjustment was applied in UUID format (e.g., 4fc06d14-0a42-41af-8d78-710b2a60947d).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN account.adjustments.adjusted_at IS '[NONE] The UTC date and time when the adjustment was applied in ISO 8601 format (e.g., 2026-02-13T08:49:44.931408+00:00).';
